{"title":"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Short_Video_solution（中文解说）in_Chinese_and_subtitle_in_English\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Short Video solution（中文解说）in Chinese and subtitle in English</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Three_perpendicular_bisectors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Three perpendicular bisectors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. The following ratio equalities hold:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e0fa91015e07f3f022d7b879a86c21313be9f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle PAD : \\angle PBA : \\angle DPA = 1 : 2 : 3 = \\angle CBP : \\angle BAP : \\angle BPC.\\]\" width=\"504\" height=\"13\" /> Prove that the following three lines meet in a point: the internal bisectors of angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe832af47de93bf6ef1d09f48a49c90c81500bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADP$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb220a462b7ed611004b6d735cf8e54236cab8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PCB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> and the perpendicular bisector of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution\">Video solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rWoA3wnXyP8\">https://youtu.be/rWoA3wnXyP8</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/bDHtM1wijbY\">https://youtu.be/bDHtM1wijbY</a> [Shorter solution, video covers all day 1 problems]\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Short_Video_solution.EF.BC.88.E4.B8.AD.E6.96.87.E8.A7.A3.E8.AF.B4.EF.BC.89in_Chinese_and_subtitle_in_English\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Short_Video_solution（中文解说）in_Chinese_and_subtitle_in_English\">Short Video solution（中文解说）in Chinese and subtitle in English</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Short Video solution（中文解说）in Chinese and subtitle in English\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WhJTaJjtjM8\">https://youtu.be/WhJTaJjtjM8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"solution_1\">solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/b/11b1f252030d63fd9169b6cd69a001cf9820d1da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP,BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> meet at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, those two lines meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b90410837ef726fe79ab0db856b6f1ccf5559e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD,BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a23366a67bb9c3c217164999ddc2098b9deed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N,M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.\n</p><p>As the problem states, denote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f515c1a639f2fd6890996fea4f182d0e9a7d1d06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{PBC}=\\alpha, \\angle{BAP}=2\\alpha, \\angle {BPC}=3\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"311\" height=\"18\" />. We can express another triple with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> as well. Since the perpendicular line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f874b39870586f0504f50a667f2bafedddf47904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d0b68865e4c7b4b1fa11fbd5a5a0c4dba2cc26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM=MP, \\angle {BPM}=\\alpha, \\angle {PMC}=2\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"18\" />, which means that points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c248c0953b35a2f4af869fef0ad76e8a7f3fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,P,M,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> are concyclic since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b378d2092368637e341d0eb50c07133a34c60e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{PAB}=\\angle{PMC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"142\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2faff38c874abd4dd4e35d5529dab87e23c73f33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,N,P,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> are concyclic as well, which means five points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a1e6f62bcf08683c48125164bb64435435c091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,N,P,M,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> are concyclic., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bcef7549bf208f7e4bb4143d280a2c25e3ea60f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ON=OP=OM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Moreover, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d32e66174e18ad49caa0bf65f0b3e64346a9f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CPM}=\\angle{CMP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"148\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/0/7e0e8007e02737c8e3db752549740d853e860270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP=CM$\" width=\"86\" height=\"12\" /> so the angle bisector if the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/9070c3b457f4514113ad5a7a1f3fcfda522c8148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MCP$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> must be the perpendicular line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a60a519059b873ec90071154f96d45f27be12c48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" />, so as the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52a73b95543fd93f7aab53b2dcdfb22bc1add249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADP}$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, which means those three lines must be concurrent at the circumcenter of the circle containing five points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a1e6f62bcf08683c48125164bb64435435c091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,N,P,M,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> as desired\n</p><p>~ bluesoul  and \"Shen Kislay kai\"\n~ edits by Pearl2008\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Three_perpendicular_bisectors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Three_perpendicular_bisectors)\">Solution 2 (Three perpendicular bisectors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Three perpendicular bisectors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2020_IMO_1a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/23/2020_IMO_1a.png/450px-2020_IMO_1a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"450\" height=\"303\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/23/2020_IMO_1a.png/675px-2020_IMO_1a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/23/2020_IMO_1a.png/900px-2020_IMO_1a.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>The essence of the proof is the replacement of the bisectors of angles by the perpendicular bisectors of the sides of the cyclic pentagon.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/940b25b815488407191668b689926f694c02b7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABP, \\angle PAD = \\alpha, OE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" /> is the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f66250786df748f8273cd4c5ecae751ece84a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f386fc0035258fe8780a97b973f9ea93679abf16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/9386ebefa540f593e809b5ac78a95455323fbd53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle APE = \\alpha,  \\angle PEA = \\pi - 2\\alpha, \\angle ABP = 2\\alpha \\implies\\]\" width=\"379\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fcab1b05f88258e88c9aeda1b0b58e20c698c612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\hspace{33mm} ABPE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"215\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/1006714997f9b7928bd3a1209442319635576a61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle PED = 2\\alpha = \\angle DPE \\implies\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"13\" />\nthe bisector of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe832af47de93bf6ef1d09f48a49c90c81500bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADP$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is the perpendicular bisector of the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f06175de06075b060abdf04ebd2ecfe88e58fc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> of the cyclic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c96d8b213016098e5c1333975852a12dfb33b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABPE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> that passes through the center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c79ddff6b45c6ad853d03d6231fdf0fba5ededb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O.$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>A similar reasoning can be done for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842bc434333e529fcc7f496f3eb39c793e762245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d33676ac63783b53331cf62d1ccf9625ef74aea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP.$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/4/984cc6b7903307691254f8e66fc45da2018a1d58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADP$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/3/0c33da4d16bf5f54ce503e3c1277199b0ff3b3d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCP$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and let them intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db22cd7f1782dab226ec344d144cc7cbcaf7212e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADP = 180^\\circ - \\angle DAP - \\angle DPA = 180^\\circ - 4\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"376\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d6412e52ede0a27380dd6febd11a841d0aea25a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADPO$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc2392a21ea406ec3563d1dc3d989c6ead32b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOP = \\frac{1}{2}\\angle ABP = 2\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"195\" height=\"38\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12b357631a344c49dc3fabc1d841ddaf4e6de453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\angle POB = \\angle BAP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"151\" height=\"38\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a781c1980ff6e4c2f2ae64ead9e4dd3e87dbb1bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/8/3f8a6c72af74a77c6abea99105aa47ad1101ad87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO = OP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/46569d6dd3fa86f698827e8de15b0480e1733d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe832af47de93bf6ef1d09f48a49c90c81500bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADP$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> and intersects at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2e03a9172e01f0bc91aca7fc99fdea67fa432e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCP$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> and intersects at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~ Ethanluyixuan2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO\" title=\"2020 IMO\">2020 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"20